# Files in this repo that are NOT part of the published site.
# The assets directory is the repository root (same as the Netlify publish
# directory), so everything not listed here would be served.
#
# Dot-paths are NOT excluded for you: the live site served /.git/config,
# /.git/logs/HEAD and /.freebuff/desktop.db (7.4 MB of local app state) until
# these lines were added — so name every one of them explicitly.
.git/
.github/
.freebuff/
.wrangler/
.vscode/
.idea/
.env
.assetsignore
brag-output/
CLAUDE.md
LICENSE
README.md
requirements.txt
scraper.py
sync_timelines.py
track_1g.py
track_permits.py
test_permits.py
test_scraper.py
test_timelines.py
test_track_1g.py
tools/
tests/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
wrangler.toml
# The function Pages compiles at deploy time. The upload is a staged copy of
# this repository, so without this rule the handler's source — the honeypot
# check, the size cap, the form names — would also be published as a file.
functions/
schema.sql
.gitignore
_headers

# Deploy files: the script that stages the upload and the staging output it
# writes (`.pages-dist/`) are development files. The assets directory is the
# repository root, so anything not listed here would be uploaded and served.
.pages-dist/
